Notes for testing:
-Fatal errors terminate the process client side after another command is attempted

CURRENT TESTS:

=====================NAM==================

==Name command==
Input command 1|NAM|4|Bob|

Result: Client names self <name>, server welcomes
them under that name.

==Duplicate name error==
Open a second terminal after first command and try 
naming the second user "Bob"

Result: A non-fatal error: "1|ERR|11|1|Name in use|"  

==Invalid Character==
Input command 1|NAM|5|B ob|

Result: Spaces is an invalid character.
        Should give a non-fatal error
        "1|ERR|11|3|Illegal character|"


==Start with non-NAM command==
Input "1|MSG|20||#all|Hello, world!|" or 
any other non-NAM command when first connecting 
as a client.

Result: A fatal error of "1|ERR|15|0|Expected NAM|"

=====================ERRORS==================

==Missing Pipe==
Input command 1|MSG|20||#all|Hello, world!

Result: A fatal error of "1|ERR|15|0|Missing Pipe|"

==Bad Version==
Input command 2|MSG|20||#all|Hello, world!

Result: A fatal error of "1|ERR|12|0|Bad Version|"

==Unknown Recipient==
Input command "1|MSG|32||Dinge|Private message to Alice|" when there is
no user known as "Dingle"

Result: A non-fatal error of "1|ERR|20|2|Unknown Recipient|"

==Unknown Type==
Input command 1|PLATE|5|what|

Result: "1|ERR|12|0|Unknown Type|"

=====================COMMANDS==================

==Public Message==
Input command: "1|MSG|20||#all|Hello, world!|"

Result: A message of "Hello, world!" received by all other
        connected clients. The sender should be whichever user
        sent the message.

==Private Message==
Input command: "1|MSG|32||Alice|Private message to Alice|"

Result: User Alice will receive a private message. No other
        user will receive the specified message.

==Set Status==
Input command: "1|SET|17|Smiling politely|"

Result: User's status will be set. ALL users will receive a
        message notification describing the status change.

==WHO (Single, Status)==
Input command: "1|WHO|6|Alice|"

Result: Granted there's a user named Alice who has a status, will
        return a message of format "... |Alice: <status>|"

==WHO (Single, No Status)==
Input command: "1|WHO|6|Alice|"

Result: Granted there's a user named Alice who has no status, will
        return a message of format "... |No status|"

==WHO (All)==
Input command: "1|WHO|5|#all|"

Result: Will return the statuses of all users with newlines between
        each user with the format "User: Status". For users without 
        a status, just their screenname will be returned.

=====================MISC==================

==Disconnect Client==

Disconnect one or more clients.

Result: This should not affect other clients or
        the server besides a notification
        that the client has disconnected on
        the server side.